## Job
This page holds the development plan for the Librarian application.
Face `04` is the overview. The parts are `plan.1` through `plan.8`. Face `05` holds the decisions.
The build happens in band `2000` members and in `app/`. Not on this page.

## Holds
The first version is the batch desk. A batch is the review queue: all model work, stops, conflicts and findings are `#NN` lines on a `05.NN`, so no work goes unseen.
Your side: see the lines that need you, stops first; reply; review solo work; see what changed and what no batch names.
The model side: start a page in an authorized band, write `01`, open a batch, add lines, report status, stop.
The files are the truth. Any index is a cache.
`reply:` is the Director's, from the user side of the desk only. In solo work a model skips the reply, works under a grant that covers its shelf or book, and writes the status after.
Models commit on work branches. Merging into `main` is the Director's.
The command on a line is its kind, from a desk command list. A command not on the list, or a write outside a grant, is kicked back.
The first version writes neither kernel.
`00.00.00.kernel` is not read. `00.00.00.kernel.draft` is the reference. `10.10.11.solo-kernel` is read before building what it already does.

## State
`05.01` and `05.02` are answered: every line has the Director's reply, transcribed from chat, and a status. Carried lines go to `05.03`.
`05.03` is open: the work that follows, and the desk, shelf and book design.
`AGENTS.003.md` is drafted beside the seat for review.

## Not
Not law. Not a kernel edit. Not a release. A line here is released only by a reply on `05.01` or `05.02`.
Not a change to any existing page or script.

